{
  "name": "sax-rs",
  "description": "A Rust wrapper for the libxml2 SAX parser that provides a streaming, event-based interface for memory-efficient XML document traversal. It abstracts low-level C callbacks through a Foreign Function Interface (FFI) and emits structured events via Rust’s channel primitives. The implementation includes support for CDATA blocks, comments, and attribute parsing, alongside detailed error reporting sourced from the underlying parser state.",
